Description: wayland: Keep committed buffers busy while unexposed
 After a frame callback timeout, safeCommit() may receive a committed
 buffer while the window is unexposed. Clearing its busy state lets the
 backing store reuse it before wl_buffer.release. The next commit is
 ignored and the window stops updating.
 .
 Keep committed buffers busy until the compositor releases them.
Author: Wu JiangYu <wujiangyu@uniontech.com>
Origin: backport, https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtbase/+/760986
Bug: https://bugreports.qt.io/browse/QTBUG-149232
Last-Update: 2026-08-18
---
--- a/src/client/qwaylandwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/client/qwaylandwindow.cpp
@@ -756,7 +756,7 @@ void QWaylandWindow::safeCommit(QWaylandBuffer *buffer, const QRegion &damage)
 {
     if (isExposed()) {
         commit(buffer, damage);
-    } else {
+    } else if (!buffer->committed()) {
         buffer->setBusy(false);
     }
 }
